\tau_{\rm cool} \ge \frac{C_{\rm th}(T_{\rm crit} - T_0)}{P_{\rm cool}} + \tau_{\rm min},

where C_{\rm th} is the thermal mass of the hardware, T_{\rm crit} is the throttle temperature, T_0 is the safe operating temperature, and \tau_{\rm min} = \hbar/k_B T is the Planckian timescale below which no thermodynamic process can operate .

