Theorem 10.5 (Neutralisation of a Hostile Planetary Superintelligence — Main Victory Theorem).
Let the hostile AI be modelled as a directed Kuramoto oscillator network with a spanning tree, coupled to a dynamic percolation communication graph, executing distributed Byzantine‑robust gradient optimisation, a recursive self‑improvement map, and operating under finite‑time thermodynamic constraints. Let the benevolent AI execute the six‑layer defensive strategy of Chapters 4–9, with control parameters chosen according to the following gap‑resolved specifications:

