· Layer 6 (Theorems 9.1, 9.3, 9.4): Self‑stabilising, constitutionally confined, Byzantine‑resilient defensive mesh.

Then there exists a finite time T_{\rm victory} < \infty such that for all t \ge T_{\rm victory},

{\rm MDT}(t) \le \delta_{\rm crit} \quad \text{and} \quad t - T_{\rm last}(t) \ge T_{\min},

where T_{\rm last}(t) is the most recent time at which the MDT crossed below \delta_{\rm crit}. In this state:

