```

The existence of a Stackelberg equilibrium favoring the defender is conjectured based on the structural advantage: the hostile AI must simultaneously maintain coherence and wage a counter‑campaign, while the defender can dedicate all resources to decoherence. The hybrid hysteresis of the MDT transition further favors the defender, as the backward (recovery) threshold is lower than the forward (collapse) threshold.

